  "goodToKnow": "Das Stadtzentrum is the city or town centre; Germans more often say die Innenstadt or, in historic towns, die Altstadt. Most German town centres have a Fußgängerzone (pedestrian zone), a post-war invention; Kassel's Treppenstraße (1953) is often called the first. Online shopping and the pandemic hit many centres, prompting talk of Innenstadtsterben (dying town centres). Plural: die Stadtzentren."
